WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:01.500
Hi, and welcome!

00:01.500 --> 00:04.517
Let me show you what Codexta is, how it works,

00:04.517 --> 00:08.650
where it's already running, and what else you could use it for.

00:10.000 --> 00:13.397
Most AI assistants trust whoever is typing.

00:13.397 --> 00:14.661
Codexta doesn't.

00:14.661 --> 00:17.427
It follows your written procedures,

00:17.427 --> 00:21.140
and locks the steps that must never be skipped.

00:22.190 --> 00:23.740
Here's how it works.

00:23.740 --> 00:26.684
A request is split into separate jobs.

00:26.684 --> 00:30.636
Each job gets only its procedure, its locked steps,

00:30.636 --> 00:32.728
and the actions it may use.

00:32.728 --> 00:36.448
The AI proposes; Codexta decides what's allowed,

00:36.448 --> 00:38.230
and records every step.

00:39.880 --> 00:42.902
Adding a process doesn't need a developer.

00:42.902 --> 00:44.701
Hand Codexta your manual,

00:44.701 --> 00:51.680
and someone with authoring permission can have it build the whole capability in one conversation.

00:52.730 --> 00:55.861
Under the hood, it's real software.

00:55.861 --> 00:59.439
Actions are C# code that Codexta writes,

00:59.439 --> 01:02.391
compiles and tests before saving.

01:02.391 --> 01:07.311
Screens are React components you preview straight away.

01:07.311 --> 01:12.500
And passwords sit in an encrypted store the AI never sees.

01:13.550 --> 01:15.722
Every change starts as a draft.

01:15.722 --> 01:16.563
You test it,

01:16.563 --> 01:20.348
and customers only see it when someone switches it on.

01:20.348 --> 01:22.240
You can always switch back.

01:23.290 --> 01:24.867
So where is it running?

01:24.867 --> 01:27.130
For a UK property-finance lender,

01:27.130 --> 01:32.410
Codexta onboards investors and takes buyers all the way to a credit decision.

01:34.260 --> 01:36.797
The buyer applies in plain English.

01:36.797 --> 01:39.407
Codexta reads every document itself,

01:39.407 --> 01:44.481
and here it caught a blank valuation and an ID in someone else's name,

01:44.481 --> 01:47.163
before anyone in credit saw the file.

01:47.163 --> 01:49.120
Ask it for the risk rating?

01:49.120 --> 01:50.570
It politely says no.

01:51.620 --> 01:55.682
Days later, the relationship manager adds a market view,

01:55.682 --> 01:57.060
in their own words.

01:57.060 --> 02:00.034
Trying to approve the request themselves?

02:00.034 --> 02:00.614
Refused.

02:00.614 --> 02:02.790
Only a credit manager decides.

02:03.840 --> 02:06.728
The credit manager gets the full assessment,

02:06.728 --> 02:10.536
with a reason for every factor, and approves in one click.

02:10.536 --> 02:13.490
The decision and its reason go on the record.

02:14.540 --> 02:20.680
And investors can't go a step further until the risk statement has been shown in full and accepted.

02:21.730 --> 02:26.361
It's the same platform everywhere: lending built straight from a manual,

02:26.361 --> 02:29.255
core banking, an online shop, a service desk,

02:29.255 --> 02:31.570
and answers from your own documents.

02:32.620 --> 02:37.611
You choose the AI, too: smaller open models on your own hardware,

02:37.611 --> 02:40.069
or the provider you already use.

02:40.069 --> 02:42.910
Codexta stays in charge of the rules.

02:43.960 --> 02:46.013
Pick one process that matters,

02:46.013 --> 02:48.751
and we'll show it working in four weeks.

02:48.751 --> 02:50.120
Thanks for watching!
